 owner_email="pihsun@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/28/623328/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I23f7d5ee9f148649afec63dabec62cbd82c36cfd" commit="29ff8e0c288bc07912402bcbeedc114c1f5080fa" commit_message="goofy_plugin: Change tooltip to use goog.ui.Tooltip.  Change tooltip to use goog.ui.Tooltip, instead of hand-written tooltip, so it can be automatically repositioned when the screen space is not enough.  BUG=None TEST=make test TEST=manually.  Change-Id: I23f7d5ee9f148649afec63dabec62cbd82c36cfd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/625646 Commit-Ready: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="625646" owner_email="pihsun@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/46/625646/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0daa4ad60383e3c9432145e94808d037ba8fd574" commit="d147c1ae3a31088879ad351c2975b6bba73a5c20" commit_message="Change Bulgaria keyboard from 102 key layout to 101 key layout.  BUG=b:18576833  TEST=manually on link  Change-Id: I0daa4ad60383e3c9432145e94808d037ba8fd574 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/613004 Commit-Ready: Yingbing Wu &lt;wuyingbing@google.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Yingbing Wu &lt;wuyingbing@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yingbing Wu &lt;wuyingbing@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yingbing Wu &lt;wuyingbing@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keigo Oka &lt;oka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shu Chen &lt;shuchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yingbing Wu &lt;wuyingbing@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yingbing Wu &lt;wuyingbing@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="613004" owner_email="wuyingbing@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/04/613004/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I79f88041a516878d49a3a15c7752edead3dd0c66" commit="00261eb91132362d6df0d2a2b760daf6fb69ccaa" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: Intel: kbl: Enabling ASRC for RT5663 codec on kabylake platform  Patch fixes cracking noise in rt5663 headphones for kbl platform by calling rt5663_sel_asrc_clk_src() for RT5663_AD_STEREO_FILTER to set ASRC.  The ASRC function is for asynchronous MCLK and LRCLK. For RT5663 ASRC should be enabled to support pcm format with 100fs. ASRC function will track i2s clock and generate corresponding system clock for codec. Calling this func helps select clock source for both RT5663_AD_STEREO_FILTER and RT5663_DA_STEREO_FILTER filters which fixes the crackling sound.  BUG=b:62555745 TEST=Verify there's no record drop on Poppy.  Signed-off-by: Harsha Priya &lt;harshapriya.n@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Shruthi Sudhakar &lt;shruthi.sudhakar@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Naveen M &lt;naveen.m@intel.com&gt; Acked-By: Vinod Koul &lt;vinod.koul@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit d46b1828406f74bc2d9ffe15e9a7b76ddbffbf7f) Signed-off-by: Hsin-Yu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I79f88041a516878d49a3a15c7752edead3dd0c66 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/627544 Commit-Ready: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="627544" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project=